PUBLIC RESPONSE: {D. Counterclockwise direction, origin near thr

The standard E. coli map order begins thr–azi–ton–lac (etc.). An Hfr origin located just proximal to thr and integrated in the counterclockwise orientation therefore transfers thr first, followed immediately by azi. Because azi enters the recipient well ahead of all subsequent markers, Azi^s is expressed for a prolonged period before the later genes arrive and recombine. No other listed origin–direction pair places azi so early in the transfer sequence.}

