PUBLIC RESPONSE: {The key detail is that azi (azis) enters the recipient and produces viable recombinants substantially earlier than any other markers tested, implying it lies immediately proximal to the origin of transfer. On the standard E. coli linkage map the gene order is thr–azi–ton–lac–pro–… . Therefore the only configuration that places azi first is an origin lying just before azi with transfer proceeding away from thr.  

Option D supplies precisely that geometry: an origin integrated near thr and transfer proceeding counterclockwise (thr → azi → ton …). All other listed origins and/or directions either place azi far from the leading end or send the chromosome in the opposite direction, so azi would appear late or not at all. Hence D is the only arrangement consistent with the data.}

}

